<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<!DOCTYPE refentry PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DocBook XML V4.2//EN"
   "http://www.oasis-open.org/docbook/xml/4.2/docbookx.dtd">
<refentry id="odffieldaudit">
  <refentryinfo>
    <productname>odfpy</productname>
  </refentryinfo>
  <refmeta>
    <refentrytitle>odffieldaudit</refentrytitle>
    <manvolnum>1</manvolnum>
    <refmiscinfo class="manual">User commands</refmiscinfo>
  </refmeta>

<refnamediv>
<refname>odffieldaudit</refname>
<refpurpose>Audit user-field declarations, references and cached display text in an ODF file</refpurpose>
</refnamediv>

<refsynopsisdiv>
<cmdsynopsis>
    <command>odffieldaudit</command>
    <arg rep="repeat">-f <replaceable>field</replaceable></arg>
    <arg>-j</arg>
    <arg>--json</arg>
    <arg>--only-issues</arg>
    <arg choice="plain" rep="repeat"><replaceable>path</replaceable></arg>
</cmdsynopsis>
</refsynopsisdiv>

<refsect1><title>Description</title>
<para>
<command>odffieldaudit</command> reports where a user field is really
used in an OpenDocument package.  Only genuine field references
(<sgmltag class="elementname">text:user-field-get</sgmltag> and
<sgmltag class="elementname">text:user-field-input</sgmltag>) are
reported; ordinary body text that merely happens to spell the same
value is not a reference and is never listed.
</para>
<para>
For every field the program shows its declarations
(<sgmltag class="elementname">text:user-field-decl</sgmltag>) with the
declared value type and value, and every reference together with the
display text cached inside the reference element.  Office applications
only refresh that cached text when fields are updated, so a string
field whose cached text differs from its declared value is flagged as
<quote>stale</quote>.  For non-string fields (numbers, dates, booleans)
a difference is reported as <quote>display-differs</quote>, because it
may simply result from number or date formatting.
</para>
<para>
References whose name has no matching declaration in the same document
scope are listed as undeclared references.  Each embedded object (the
<quote>Object N</quote> folders, including nested objects) is an
independent document, so a field inside an object is resolved against
that object's own declarations only, never against the host document.
</para>
<para>
Every reported occurrence carries a location of the form
<replaceable>part</replaceable>:<replaceable>line</replaceable>:<replaceable>column</replaceable>
that points at the opening tag of the element, for example
<filename>styles.xml:11:11</filename> for a field used in a page header.
</para>
<para>
<quote>Path</quote> is assumed to be an OpenDocument file of text,
spreadsheet or presentation type.  More than one path may be given so
that several files can be audited in one batch; a file that cannot be
opened is reported as an error while the remaining files are still
processed.
</para>
</refsect1>

<refsect1><title>Options</title>
<variablelist>

<varlistentry>
<term>-f <replaceable>field</replaceable></term>
<listitem>
<para>
Restrict the audit to the named user field.  The option may be given
more than once.  By default all user fields are audited.
</para>
</listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry>
<term>-j</term>
<term>--json</term>
<listitem>
<para>
Emit machine readable JSON instead of the human readable text report.
</para>
</listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry>
<term>--only-issues</term>
<listitem>
<para>
Only list undeclared references and references whose cached display
text differs from the declared value.
</para>
</listitem>
</varlistentry>

</variablelist>
</refsect1>

<refsect1><title>Exit status</title>
<para>
The program exits with status <returnvalue>1</returnvalue> when at least
one undeclared reference or stale string field was found, and
<returnvalue>0</returnvalue> otherwise.  Non-string
<quote>display-differs</quote> findings do not change the exit status on
their own.
</para>
</refsect1>

<refsect1><title>Example</title>
<screen>
odffieldaudit -f 批号 document.odt
odffieldaudit --json --only-issues document.odt
</screen>
</refsect1>

<refsect1><title>See Also</title>
<para>
<command>odfuserfield</command>(1)
</para>
</refsect1>

</refentry>
